hit → hot → lot → log → cog
⏱ Time Complexity

Let:

N = number of words

L = length of word

Generating neighbors:

O(N * L * 26)

Overall:

≈ O(N * L * 26)

Backtracking cost depends on number of paths.

📦 Space Complexity
O(N)
⚡ Why Simple DFS Fails?

Because:

DFS explores deeper before shortest guarantee

Might return longer paths

Only BFS guarantees minimum depth first.

🎯 Interview Summary Answer

Use BFS to compute shortest path levels and build a directed graph of shortest transitions. Then use DFS/backtracking to reconstruct all shortest sequences.

